our community has lost long-time las  vegas resident steven shore  he was a former news reporter anchor  right here at klas-tv  and had many accomplishments to his name  he was most  recognized as the long-time spokesman  for cox communications  where he previously served as vp of  public and government affairs  kirsten joyce joins us now with a bit  more brian  received a statement from the shore  family saying in part that he passed  away yesterday at the age of 74 from  natural causes  the family says over the past 40 years  steve was widely recognized for his  tireless and lengthy community  involvement  with civic organizations youth groups  and at one point  had served on the board of directors of  20 local non-profits  we've got a picture of steve when he  worked here at klas in the 1980s as an  investigative reporter and then went on  to anchor receiving many awards for  journalism  also he was a familiar face as the mc of  best in show for many many years  president peter guzman of the latin  chamber of commerce says steve had a  35-year history as a volunteer  with the chamber i always loved picking  his brain and hearing about  old vegas because i love old vegas and  he just had a way of doing it with  dignity and kindness and  even when he scolded you and he had he  scolded me a couple times on  you know his thoughts on certain things  that i was doing at the chamber and  how i could be doing it better he always  did it with dignity and kindness  when you lose good people like this  giants in our community  guys who really uh steve had a way of  connecting with grassroots and  and ceos i mean you know he treated  everybody the same and  i always appreciated that about him and  it just hits home when you lose a kind  man like that uh  one of our own and his family said he  was most proud of his  wife his sons and grandchildren and all  the students at his namesake steve shore  elementary school  donations and funeral services are still  pending  brian and cure we heard from a number of  people today including friend and  former anchor gary waddell gary said i  worked with steve a number of times when  he was at channel 8 and when he was  doing things  in our community the magnitude of his  community involvement in las vegas  is truly amazing he was always kind and  always a gentleman  he will truly be missed by all in  southern nevada and leaves a vacancy in  this  community that will be impossible for  one person to fill  rest in peace my friend rest in peace
 

